B.ajh=new A.c9("1. Effective date and scope","Effective 23 September 2026. Version 2026-09-23.\n\nThis Privacy & Data Protection Notice applies to PASSAGE accounts, child profiles, rider/driver vetting, trips, journey verification, location features, notifications, support and related services. It is designed for Uganda and takes account of the Uganda Data Protection and Privacy Act, 2019 and the Data Protection and Privacy Regulations, 2021.")
B.ajy=new A.c9("2. Our child-data commitment","PASSAGE treats child information as high-risk operational information. We collect only information needed for a defined purpose, restrict access according to role and need, avoid unnecessary public disclosure and use child information primarily for safety, transport, verification, support and legal obligations.\n\nA child\u2019s information is not used for unrelated advertising or sold.")
B.ajE=new A.c9("3. Who is responsible for the data","PASSAGE Mobility operates the PASSAGE service in Uganda. The exact legal entity and registered physical address of the operator should be stated in the operator\u2019s public legal details and PDPO registration records.\n\nPASSAGE will designate and publish a Data Protection Officer/contact in accordance with applicable Ugandan requirements. Privacy requests are handled through the PASSAGE in-app privacy/support channel.")
B.ak0=new A.c9("4. Information we collect","Parent/guardian data may include name, phone number, email, account details and information needed to manage children and trips.\n\nChild data may include name, school, grade/class, school identifier where applicable, date of birth where provided, photograph, emergency contact, authorised guardian details, trip information, verification events and journey/location information associated with a trip.\n\nDriver/rider data may include name, phone/email, National ID number, residential area, boda boda stage/association, years of commercial riding, passport photograph, National ID images, riding permit, vehicle information, approval status, trip activity and location information.\n\nTechnical information may include device, application, authentication, diagnostic, security and service-use information reasonably required to operate and protect PASSAGE.")
B.ajv=new A.c9("5. Location data","PASSAGE may process precise location when required for dispatch, pickup/drop-off, live journey monitoring, emergency response, journey verification, safety alerts, dispute handling and service operation.\n\nLocation access should be limited to the relevant operational purpose and retained only for as long as needed for that purpose, legal obligations, safety investigations or legitimate records. PASSAGE does not use a person\u2019s location as general-purpose surveillance.")
B.ajj=new A.c9("6. Photographs and identity documents","Driver identity documents and photographs are collected for vetting, identity verification, safety and legal/compliance purposes. Child photographs are collected for child identification and safety workflows.\n\nThese records are stored in protected storage with access controls. They are not intended for public display. Access is limited to authorised people and service providers who need the information for the stated purposes.")
B.ajF=new A.c9("7. Why we process data","PASSAGE may process personal data to create and manage accounts; register and safeguard children; verify parent/guardian authority; vet riders/drivers; match and dispatch trips; monitor journeys; verify pickup/drop-off; communicate trip information; respond to emergencies; investigate safety incidents and misuse; provide support; secure the platform; meet legal obligations; resolve disputes; maintain necessary business records; and improve the service using proportionate and privacy-preserving methods.")
B.ajo=new A.c9("8. Lawful basis","Depending on the processing, PASSAGE may rely on prior consent, performance of a contract or steps requested before a contract, compliance with a legal obligation, protection of a person\u2019s vital interests or another lawful basis recognised by applicable law.\n\nFor child personal data, PASSAGE requires prior consent of a parent, guardian or other person with authority to make decisions for the child except where processing is otherwise permitted by law. The consent is recorded with the policy version and server timestamp.")
B.ajt=new A.c9("9. Child-data consent","Before a child profile is created, the parent/guardian must affirm that they have authority to provide the child\u2019s information and must expressly consent to PASSAGE processing the child\u2019s information for the purposes described in this Notice.\n\nThe consent record includes the child account identifier, policy version and server-generated acceptance time. Consent is separate from general acceptance of the Terms and Privacy Notice.")
B.ak1=new A.c9("10. Access to child information","Child information is shared only with people or systems that need it for the service and safety. Depending on the trip, this may include the parent/guardian, the assigned approved rider/driver, authorised PASSAGE operations staff, relevant school or institutional partners, emergency responders or service providers acting for PASSAGE.\n\nA rider/driver should receive only information necessary to perform the assigned journey. Access is not a general right to browse children\u2019s records.")
B.ajJ=new A.c9("11. Sharing and disclosure","PASSAGE may disclose information where necessary to provide the service, protect a child or person, investigate fraud or safety incidents, comply with law, respond to lawful requests, or use a contracted processor.\n\nPASSAGE does not sell personal data. PASSAGE does not disclose child information for unrelated advertising. Any partner or processor handling personal data on PASSAGE\u2019s behalf should be subject to appropriate contractual and technical safeguards.")
B.ajz=new A.c9("12. Schools and institutional partners","Where PASSAGE works with a school or institution, the parties will define their respective responsibilities for personal data. Depending on the arrangement, a school or institution may be a controller, joint controller or processor for particular processing activities.\n\nAccess should be limited to the information and functions necessary for the agreed service and child-safety purpose.")
B.ajI=new A.c9("13. Security","PASSAGE uses technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risks of the information processed. These may include encrypted network transport, protected cloud storage, authentication controls, row-level access controls, least-privilege access, protected document storage, validation, monitoring, backups and controlled administrative access.\n\nNo internet service can guarantee absolute security. PASSAGE will investigate suspected personal-data incidents, contain risk, preserve evidence and make notifications required by applicable law.")
B.ajK=new A.c9("14. Retention and deletion","PASSAGE does not intend to retain personal data longer than necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law, contract, safety investigation, dispute resolution or another lawful purpose.\n\nWhen the applicable retention period expires, records should be securely deleted or de-identified in a manner that prevents reconstruction where required. Specific retention schedules will be applied by data category and operational need.")
B.ajG=new A.c9("15. Your data-protection rights","Subject to applicable law and lawful exceptions, data subjects may have rights to access personal data, request correction of inaccurate information, object to certain processing, request deletion where permitted, and exercise other rights provided by Ugandan data-protection law.\n\nRequests may require identity verification to prevent unauthorised disclosure. PASSAGE will handle valid requests within applicable legal time limits.")
B.ajB=new A.c9("16. Children\u2019s requests and safeguarding","A child may raise a privacy or safety concern through a parent/guardian, authorised adult or appropriate PASSAGE safeguarding channel. PASSAGE will consider the child\u2019s interests and applicable law when responding.\n\nA privacy request must not be used to conceal an immediate safety risk. Where disclosure is lawfully necessary to protect a child or comply with law, PASSAGE may retain or disclose relevant information notwithstanding an ordinary deletion request.")
B.ajM=new A.c9("17. International processing","PASSAGE may use cloud or service providers located outside Uganda. Where personal data is processed or stored outside Uganda, PASSAGE will apply the safeguards required by Ugandan law, including assessing whether the destination provides adequate protection or obtaining consent where the law permits or requires that approach.")
B.ajs=new A.c9("18. Cookies and technical information","Web and app services may use strictly necessary storage, session technologies, diagnostics and security logs to authenticate users, remember settings, prevent abuse and maintain service reliability. Optional analytics or similar technologies should be used only where appropriately configured and disclosed.")
B.aji=new A.c9("19. Automated decisions and profiling","PASSAGE may use automated rules for operational tasks such as dispatch, matching, fraud or abuse controls. PASSAGE will not rely solely on an automated process to make a decision producing a legal or similarly significant effect on a person without appropriate safeguards and human review where required by law or fairness considerations.")
B.ajS=new A.c9("20. Advertising","PASSAGE does not sell child information or use child profiles for behavioural advertising. Any future marketing or advertising activity involving personal data will be assessed for legality, necessity, consent requirements and child-safety implications before deployment.")
B.ajV=new A.c9("21. Data minimisation and privacy by design","PASSAGE aims to collect the minimum information needed for each feature, use privacy-protective defaults, limit access by role, avoid unnecessary location precision or retention, and review new high-risk processing before launch.\n\nWhere processing is likely to create a high risk to people\u2019s rights and freedoms, PASSAGE will conduct an appropriate Data Protection Impact Assessment and implement necessary safeguards.")
B.ajw=new A.c9("22. Third-party links and services","PASSAGE may link to third-party services such as mapping, authentication or support providers. Those services may have their own privacy terms. PASSAGE remains responsible for the personal-data processing it controls, while third-party providers may have separate responsibilities for data they process independently.")
B.ajR=new A.c9("23. Policy changes and version control","This Notice may change when PASSAGE\u2019s services, providers, security practices or applicable law change. The effective date and policy version are displayed in the app. Material changes requiring renewed consent will trigger a new acceptance record rather than silently treating continued use as consent.")
B.ajY=new A.c9("24. Complaints and the PDPO","Privacy concerns should first be raised through PASSAGE\u2019s privacy/support channel so the issue can be investigated and corrected where appropriate.\n\nA data subject may also contact the Personal Data Protection Office of Uganda, the independent data-protection authority responsible for overseeing the Data Protection and Privacy Act.")
B.ajr=new A.c9("25. Contact and privacy requests","Use the PASSAGE in-app privacy/support channel for access, correction, deletion, consent, child-data or other privacy requests. Do not send a child\u2019s National ID, full home address or other highly sensitive material through an unsecured public channel unless PASSAGE specifically instructs you to do so.\n\nPASSAGE Mobility is the service name used for the Ugandan PASSAGE service. The operator's registered legal name, physical address and Data Protection Officer contact details must remain consistent with the operator's current PDPO registration and public legal details.\n\nIf a concern cannot be resolved directly with PASSAGE, the Personal Data Protection Office of Uganda can be contacted through its official channels: info@pdpo.go.ug, +256 417 801 008 / +256 417 801 009 / +256 417 801 011.")
