B.ajH=new A.c9("1. About PASSAGE","PASSAGE is a child-focused mobility and journey-verification service designed to help parents and authorised adults arrange and monitor safer journeys for children. PASSAGE may provide account management, child profiles, driver/rider vetting, trip requests, assignment, journey status, location tracking, pickup/drop-off verification, emergency reporting and related notifications.\n\nPASSAGE is a technology service. A transport journey is carried out by the approved driver/rider assigned to the trip. PASSAGE does not replace a parent or guardian\u2019s responsibility for decisions concerning a child.")
B.ajW=new A.c9("2. Child safety and best interests","PASSAGE is designed around the safety, dignity and privacy of children. Information about a child must be provided only by a parent, guardian or another person with lawful authority to make decisions for that child. Users must not create a child profile without that authority.\n\nWhere a safety issue, safeguarding concern, emergency or suspected misuse arises, PASSAGE may take reasonable protective steps, including restricting accounts, pausing a journey, contacting emergency or safeguarding contacts, or sharing information where lawful and necessary to protect a child or comply with the law.")
B.ajk=new A.c9("3. Eligibility and accounts","Parent/guardian accounts are intended for adults or persons with legal authority to arrange a child\u2019s journey. Rider/driver accounts are subject to identity, document and safety vetting and remain pending until approved by PASSAGE.\n\nYou must provide accurate information, keep your contact details current, protect your authentication credentials and immediately report suspected unauthorised account use. You may not create an account for another person without authority or impersonate another person.")
B.ajm=new A.c9("4. Child registration","A parent/guardian may provide a child\u2019s name, school, grade/class, school identifier where applicable, date of birth where needed, photograph, emergency contact and authorised-guardian details. A passport photograph is required where the PASSAGE workflow requires it.\n\nA PASSAGE QR/wearable identifier is not automatically issued merely because a child profile is created. It is assigned later through the approved issuance process.")
B.ak_=new A.c9("5. Parental and guardian authority","By registering a child, you confirm that you are the child\u2019s parent, guardian or other person authorised to make the relevant decisions. You are responsible for the accuracy of the child\u2019s information and for obtaining any consent required from another parent, guardian or authorised person.\n\nYou must not upload another person\u2019s personal information unless you have a lawful basis or authority to do so.")
B.ajx=new A.c9("6. Driver/rider registration and vetting","A driver/rider applicant may be required to provide a National ID number, residential area, boda boda stage or association, years of commercial riding experience, passport photograph, National ID front and back and riding permit, together with any additional information reasonably required for safety and legal compliance.\n\nSubmission does not mean approval. PASSAGE may review documents, verify information, reject an application, suspend access or request updated documents. A pending rider must not provide PASSAGE child transport services.")
B.ajT=new A.c9("7. Driver/rider conduct","Approved riders must comply with applicable Ugandan traffic, road-safety and child-protection requirements and with PASSAGE operational instructions. A rider must not knowingly deviate from an authorised trip for an improper purpose, expose a child to avoidable danger, share child information with unauthorised people, or use PASSAGE information for unrelated purposes.\n\nPASSAGE may suspend or terminate access where safety, integrity, compliance or safeguarding requires it.")
B.ajC=new A.c9("8. Transport mode and trip requests","When requesting a trip, the parent/guardian selects the transport mode offered by PASSAGE, currently Boda boda or Car. The selected mode is part of the trip request and may affect matching and dispatch.\n\nTrip notes are intended for relevant rider instructions or special requests. Users must not place unnecessary sensitive information in trip notes.")
B.ajX=new A.c9("9. Location and journey monitoring","PASSAGE may process pickup and drop-off locations, journey status and, where enabled for an active trip, driver/rider location information to support dispatch, journey monitoring, pickup/drop-off verification, emergency response, notifications, dispute handling, safety and service improvement.\n\nLocation access is not a general licence to monitor people outside the purposes described in the Privacy Notice. PASSAGE seeks to minimise location collection and access to what is necessary for the service.")
B.ajQ=new A.c9("10. Pickup, drop-off and verification","PASSAGE may use child tags, QR identifiers, trip events, PINs, timestamps, location information or other verification controls to reduce the risk of a child being collected or released to an unauthorised person.\n\nParents/guardians must keep verification information confidential. Riders must not bypass or falsify a verification step.")
B.ajU=new A.c9("11. Emergency situations","The service may provide emergency reporting and escalation features. In an actual or suspected emergency, PASSAGE may process and disclose relevant information to emergency responders, guardians, authorised staff, schools or other persons where reasonably necessary and lawful to protect a child or person.\n\nUsers should contact the appropriate emergency service directly where immediate physical intervention is required.")
B.ajl=new A.c9("12. Communications and notifications","PASSAGE may send service messages by available channels, including account notices, trip updates, safety alerts, driver/rider status, pickup/drop-off notifications and important policy changes. Transactional safety communications may be necessary for the service and may not be treated as optional marketing.")
B.ajZ=new A.c9("13. Third-party services","PASSAGE may rely on carefully selected technology providers for hosting, authentication, storage, maps, notifications, analytics, communications and other infrastructure. Such providers may process information on PASSAGE\u2019s behalf under appropriate contractual and security controls.\n\nPASSAGE does not sell personal data.")
B.ajD=new A.c9("14. Payments","If payment functionality is introduced, applicable payment terms, prices and payment-provider notices will be presented before payment is requested. Payment providers may process payment information under their own terms and privacy notices. PASSAGE will not ask users to place full payment-card secrets in ordinary trip notes or support messages.")
B.ajp=new A.c9("15. Prohibited use","Users must not use PASSAGE to harass, threaten, stalk, discriminate against, exploit or endanger a child or another person; submit false identity or safety information; circumvent verification; access another user\u2019s data; interfere with the service; upload unlawful or malicious material; or use child information for advertising, profiling or unrelated commercial activity without a lawful basis.")
B.aju=new A.c9("16. Suspension and termination","PASSAGE may restrict, suspend or terminate an account, trip, driver approval or access where required for safety, safeguarding, fraud prevention, legal compliance, investigation, breach of these Terms or protection of the service.\n\nWhere practicable, PASSAGE will provide an explanation appropriate to the circumstances. Emergency protective action may be taken first where delay could increase risk.")
B.ajO=new A.c9("17. Service availability and limitations","PASSAGE uses reasonable measures to maintain service availability but does not promise uninterrupted operation. Mobile networks, GPS, devices, electricity, cloud services, mapping services and other infrastructure can fail or become inaccurate.\n\nUsers must use reasonable judgement and must not treat a GPS position, ETA or digital status as a guarantee of physical safety.")
B.ajA=new A.c9("18. Responsibility for transport","The parent/guardian remains responsible for deciding whether a journey is appropriate for the child and for providing accurate pickup, drop-off, emergency and special-request information. Drivers/riders remain responsible for complying with applicable transport and road-safety obligations.\n\nNothing in these Terms removes a right or obligation that cannot lawfully be excluded under Ugandan law.")
B.ajL=new A.c9("19. User-submitted information","You remain responsible for the information you submit. You grant PASSAGE the limited rights necessary to store, process, transmit and display that information to provide the requested service, protect users, meet legal obligations and operate the platform.\n\nDo not upload information that is unrelated to the service or that you are not authorised to provide.")
B.ajN=new A.c9("20. Intellectual property","PASSAGE software, branding, interface elements, documentation and other platform materials are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Users receive a limited, non-exclusive right to use the service for its intended purpose. You may not copy, reverse engineer, resell or commercially exploit PASSAGE materials except where law permits.")
B.ajq=new A.c9("21. Feedback","Feedback may be used by PASSAGE to improve the service. Do not include confidential child information in general feedback unless it is necessary for a safety or support request.")
B.ajP=new A.c9("22. Changes to these Terms","PASSAGE may update these Terms when the service, law, safety requirements or business arrangements change. The current version and effective date will be displayed in the app. Where a change materially affects consent or rights, PASSAGE will seek renewed acceptance where required by law.")
B.ajn=new A.c9("23. Governing law and complaints","These Terms are intended to operate under the laws of Uganda, subject to any mandatory rights or protections that apply to a user. Privacy complaints may be raised through PASSAGE\u2019s privacy/support channel and, where appropriate, with the Personal Data Protection Office of Uganda.")
